<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Friday 95,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Friday 95,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipt estimates:</p>
<p>Friday:   95,000  Wk ago: 91,000   Yr ago: 100,000</p>
<p>Saturday: 15,000  Wk ago: 15,000   Yr ago:  21,000</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts $0.50 per cwt lower, compared mid-session Thursday. Trade slow to moderate for light to moderate demand and offerings.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    55.00 -56.50	   56.00 -57.50</p>
<p>liberal volume	 55.50 -56.00	   56.50 -57.00</p>
<p>few			57.00		    58.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    54.00 -56.50	   54.50 -57.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    54.00 -56.50	   54.50 -57.50</p>
<p>Sows:  steady to 1.00 higher.</p>
<p>US 1-3  300-450 lbs. 43.00 -45.00	   44.00 -46.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   44.00 -47.00	   44.00 -47.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    47.00 -52.00	   47.00 -53.00</p>
<p>Compared to last week: Barrows and Gilts $0.50-1.00 lower. Sows 1.00-2.00 higher.  Receipts this week 518,000 last week 486,000, last year 529,000. Barrows and Gilts average weight for week ending April 26, 1997  253.3 lbs compared to 253.4 lbs previous week 248.5 lbs last year.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
